  "title": "Why That 0% Interest Offer Could Backfire\u2014Big Time",
  "date": "2025-06-17T14:31:16.009Z",
  "content": {
    "text": "96\n\n Why That 0% Interest Offer Could Backfire\u2014Big Time\nHi Sara,\nLet\u2019s talk about something that gets ignored way too often in deal negotiations: interest rates on seller financing.\nYes, I know. Not exactly a crowd-pleaser at cocktail hour. But if you\u2019re buying or selling a business and you throw out a 0% interest promissory note thinking it\u2019s no big deal\u2026 you might want to sit down.\nHere\u2019s the deal:\nThe IRS has this little thing called the Applicable Federal Rate (AFR). It's their way of saying, \u201cIf you lend someone money, we expect you to earn a certain minimum interest\u2014or we\u2019ll tax you like you did.\u201d\nSo what happens if the AFR is 4% and your deal includes a 2% interest rate on a $100,000 note?\nThe seller only pockets $2,000 in actual interest\u2014but Uncle Sam taxes them like they made $4,000. That phantom $2,000? Still taxed. That\u2019s called imputed interest income, and it\u2019s about as fun as it sounds.\nNow imagine that same problem with a 0% loan on, say, a $500,000 balance. The tax hit alone can be thousands of dollars\u2026 for income the seller never actually received.\nWhy This Matters:\nWhen buyers pitch 0% interest seller notes, they\u2019re not just asking for a sweet deal\u2014they\u2019re handing the seller a tax bill on top of the loan risk and inflation erosion. It\u2019s like borrowing their car, returning it with no gas, and handing them a parking ticket for good measure.\nYou can do better.\nSavvy buyers will either:\nOffer interest at the current AFR (Google it\u2014rates are public),\n\nOr at least understand the risk they\u2019re asking the seller to shoulder and explain why the structure makes sense.\n\nAnd if this is the first time you\u2019re hearing about AFR or imputed interest? Please don\u2019t toss a 0% loan in your LOI like it\u2019s a hot tip from a Reddit thread.\nBottom line: If you want seller financing to actually work, make it fair. Or at the very least, don\u2019t make it tax-punitive.\nReady to structure smarter offers that actually get accepted?\nCheck out Deal Academy. It\u2019s where I help real buyers and sellers stop learning lessons the hard (and expensive) way.\nTo not getting side-eyed at the negotiation table,\nSara Sharp\nPartner, SK&S Law Group\nFounder, Deal Academy\nP.S. If you're looking to buy or sell an accounting firm, and want me to keep an eye out for you, fill out this form here.\n\n For more helpful lessons from Deal Academy, check out our Dealmakers Youtube Channel where you'll find Sara's Weekly Wine Down, where she talks about what she's seen in the industry this week and interviews with M&A Experts and Dealmakers.\nYou can check out some recent Dealmakers YouTube videos by clicking the images below.\n\n Copyright \u00a9 2025\u00a0 Someday Consultants, All rights reserved. \n\n Our e-mail address is:\ninfo@dealacademy.org\n\n Want to change how you receive these emails?\n You can unsubscribe from this list.",
